<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles XIV John</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1763">1763</a>–<a href="/years/1844">1844</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Jean-Baptiste Bernadotte, Charles III John of Norway</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles XIV John, born Jean-Baptiste Bernadotte, was a French marshal under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> who was elected heir to the Swedish throne in 1810. He joined the coalition against Napoleon and forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> to cede <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in 1814. King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and Norway from 1818, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bernadotte">Bernadotte dynasty</a> and kept Sweden at peace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-xiv-john.jpg" alt="Charles XIV John" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CarlsSston · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_XIV_Johan,_Sveriges_och_Norges_konung._Portr%C3%A4tt_av_Frederic_Westin,_cirka_1843._-_kopia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
